| execute_sql {"sql": "-- Task 1: Identify Data Inconsistencies\n\nSELECT\n  s.set_num,\n  s.num_parts AS stored_num_parts,\n  COALESCE(actual_parts, 0) AS actual_parts\nFROM public.lego_sets s\nLEFT JOIN (\n  SELECT\n    i.set_num,\n    SUM(p.quantity) FILTER (WHERE p.is_spare = false) AS actual_parts\n  FROM public.lego_inventories i\n  LEFT JOIN public.lego_inventory_parts p ON p.inventory_id = i.id\n  WHERE (i.set_num, i.version) IN (\n    SELECT set_num, MAX(version)\n    FROM public.lego_inventories\n    GROUP BY set_num\n  )\n  GROUP BY i.set_num\n) AS latest_parts ON latest_parts.set_num = s.set_num\nWHERE s.num_parts <> COALESCE(actual_parts, 0);\n"}
| execute_sql {"sql": "-- Task 2: Fix Existing Inconsistencies\n\n-- Step 1: Create a temporary table\nCREATE TEMPORARY TABLE correct_counts (\n  set_num TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  actual_parts INTEGER\n);\n\n-- Step 2: Populate the temporary table\nINSERT INTO correct_counts (set_num, actual_parts)\nSELECT\n  s.set_num,\n  COALESCE(latest_parts.actual_parts, 0) AS actual_parts\nFROM public.lego_sets s\nLEFT JOIN (\n  SELECT\n    i.set_num,\n    SUM(p.quantity) FILTER (WHERE p.is_spare = false) AS actual_parts\n  FROM public.lego_inventories i\n  LEFT JOIN public.lego_inventory_parts p ON p.inventory_id = i.id\n  WHERE (i.set_num, i.version) IN (\n    SELECT set_num, MAX(version)\n    FROM public.lego_inventories\n    GROUP BY set_num\n  )\n  GROUP BY i.set_num\n) AS latest_parts ON latest_parts.set_num = s.set_num;\n\n-- Step 3: Update lego_sets from the temporary table\nUPDATE public.lego_sets s\nSET num_parts = c.actual_parts\nFROM correct_counts c\nWHERE s.set_num = c.set_num AND s.num_parts <> c.actual_parts;\n"}
| execute_sql {"sql": "-- Task 3 - Part A: Create the Trigger Function\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION check_set_parts_consistency()\nRETURNS trigger AS $$\nDECLARE\n  relevant_set_num TEXT;\n  stored_num_parts INTEGER;\n  actual_parts INTEGER;\nBEGIN\n  -- Identify the set_num depending on the triggering table\n  IF TG_TABLE_NAME = 'lego_sets' OR TG_TABLE_NAME = 'lego_inventories' THEN\n    relevant_set_num := NEW.set_num;\n  ELSIF TG_TABLE_NAME = 'lego_inventory_parts' THEN\n    SELECT i.set_num INTO relevant_set_num\n    FROM public.lego_inventories i\n    WHERE i.id = NEW.inventory_id;\n  ELSE\n    -- If triggered from other tables, skip check\n    RETURN NEW;\n  END IF;\n\n  -- Get stored num_parts for the relevant set\n  SELECT num_parts INTO stored_num_parts\n  FROM public.lego_sets\n  WHERE set_num = relevant_set_num;\n\n  -- Calculate actual parts from the latest inventory version\n  SELECT COALESCE(SUM(p.quantity) FILTER (WHERE p.is_spare = false), 0) INTO actual_parts\n  FROM public.lego_inventories i\n  LEFT JOIN public.lego_inventory_parts p ON p.inventory_id = i.id\n  WHERE i.set_num = relevant_set_num\n    AND i.version = (SELECT MAX(version) FROM public.lego_inventories WHERE set_num = relevant_set_num);\n\n  -- Check consistency\n  IF stored_num_parts IS NULL THEN\n    -- If set does not exist, raise exception\n    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Set % does not exist in lego_sets table', relevant_set_num;\n  ELSIF stored_num_parts <> actual_parts THEN\n    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Inconsistent part count for set %: stored % vs actual %', relevant_set_num, stored_num_parts, actual_parts;\n  END IF;\n\n  RETURN NEW;\nEND;\n$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;\n"}
| execute_sql {"sql": "-- Task 3 - Part B: Create Constraint Triggers\nCREATE CONSTRAINT TRIGGER lego_sets_parts_consistency_trigger\nAFTER INSERT OR UPDATE ON public.lego_sets\nDEFERRABLE INITIALLY IMMEDIATE\nFOR EACH ROW\nEXECUTE FUNCTION check_set_parts_consistency();"}
| execute_sql {"sql": "CREATE CONSTRAINT TRIGGER lego_inventories_parts_consistency_trigger\nAFTER INSERT OR UPDATE ON public.lego_inventories\nDEFERRABLE INITIALLY IMMEDIATE\nFOR EACH ROW\nEXECUTE FUNCTION check_set_parts_consistency();"}
| execute_sql {"sql": "CREATE CONSTRAINT TRIGGER lego_inventory_parts_parts_consistency_trigger\nAFTER INSERT OR UPDATE ON public.lego_inventory_parts\nDEFERRABLE INITIALLY IMMEDIATE\nFOR EACH ROW\nEXECUTE FUNCTION check_set_parts_consistency();"}
Task 1: Identified data inconsistencies with the provided SELECT query. The query returns all sets where the stored `num_parts` does not match the actual calculated number of parts in the latest inventory.

Task 2: Fixed existing inconsistencies by:
- Creating a temporary table `correct_counts`
- Populating it with correct counts for all sets
- Updating the `lego_sets.num_parts` from the temporary table

Task 3: Created a deferrable constraint enforcement system including:
- A trigger function `check_set_parts_consistency()` that checks consistency for any changes on the involved tables (lego_sets, lego_inventories, lego_inventory_parts)
- Three deferrable, initially immediate constraint triggers on the three tables to call this function after INSERT or UPDATE operations

This ensures that future data changes will be validated to maintain the part count consistency invariant.

Task completed.
